## Purpose

Integrate the FlashInfer CuTeDSL BF16 low-latency dense GEMM from
[flashinfer-ai/flashinfer#4266](https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/4266).


This PR:

- adds `flashinfer_cutedsl` as an opt-in `--linear-backend`;
- uses `flashinfer.mm_bf16(..., backend="cute-dsl")` for eligible unquantized
  BF16 GEMMs on SM100-family GPUs;
- limits the FlashInfer path to supported low-M shapes and falls back to the
  existing PyTorch linear path otherwise;
- preserves the configured backend across model construction and compilation;
- includes an M=32 FlashInfer autotune warmup when the configured
